WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.120
"Is Shrimp Bad for Cholesterol and Heart Disease?"

00:00:07.120 --> 00:00:09.920
When people were randomized
to consume shellfish

00:00:09.920 --> 00:00:14.000
or the same amount by protein
of meat, cheese, and eggs,

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:18.240
surprisingly, shrimp did not
lower their LDL cholesterol,

00:00:18.240 --> 00:00:21.680
perhaps because shrimp is
so high in dietary cholesterol.

00:00:21.680 --> 00:00:24.240
Shrimp is exceedingly low
in saturated fat,

00:00:24.240 --> 00:00:26.080
like, 30 times less
than other meat,

00:00:26.080 --> 00:00:28.320
but it has about
twice as much cholesterol,

00:00:28.320 --> 00:00:31.040
which dietary guidelines
recommend we reduce in our diet

00:00:31.040 --> 00:00:33.840
to as low as possible.

00:00:33.840 --> 00:00:35.600
If people are given
the same amount of cholesterol

00:00:35.600 --> 00:00:38.000
in the form of shrimp or eggs,

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:40.720
they get about the same rise
in LDL cholesterol,

00:00:40.720 --> 00:00:43.440
which alone could increase our
lifetime risk of heart disease

00:00:43.440 --> 00:00:45.280
by about 15%.

00:00:45.280 --> 00:00:47.840
But there are a lot more people
eating two eggs a day

00:00:47.840 --> 00:00:50.960
than, like, 11 ounces (310 g)
of shrimp a day.

00:00:50.960 --> 00:00:53.680
And eating wild-caught
cold-water prawns,

00:00:53.680 --> 00:00:55.280
a different species of shrimp,

00:00:55.280 --> 00:00:58.240
doesn’t appear to budge
LDL cholesterol much at all.

00:00:58.240 --> 00:00:59.840
Unfortunately,
about one in three shrimp

00:00:59.840 --> 00:01:02.000
in the grocery store
is mislabeled,

00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:04.640
so, it may be hard
to pick and choose.

00:01:04.640 --> 00:01:06.720
There is another way
meat may contribute

00:01:06.720 --> 00:01:08.560
to heart disease risk.

00:01:08.560 --> 00:01:10.640
In certain areas
of the United States

00:01:10.640 --> 00:01:11.600
and around the world,

00:01:11.600 --> 00:01:14.080
getting bitten
by certain types of ticks

00:01:14.080 --> 00:01:16.720
can make you allergic to meat.

00:01:16.720 --> 00:01:17.840
In some parts of the U.S.

00:01:17.840 --> 00:01:19.600
where the lone star tick
is endemic,

00:01:19.600 --> 00:01:22.480
as many as 20% of people
have allergy-type antibodies

00:01:22.480 --> 00:01:24.640
against meat
in their bloodstream.

00:01:24.640 --> 00:01:27.760
But the prevalence
of clinically appreciated

00:01:27.760 --> 00:01:31.760
allergic symptoms is thought
to be at least 10-fold less.

00:01:31.760 --> 00:01:34.400
So, they’re sensitized to meat,
but when they eat it,

00:01:34.400 --> 00:01:35.920
they don’t exhibit
any symptoms.

00:01:35.920 --> 00:01:38.720
And because of that,
they continue to eat meat.

00:01:38.720 --> 00:01:41.840
But what if that’s causing
inflammation inside their bodies

00:01:41.840 --> 00:01:43.520
even if they don’t feel it?

00:01:43.520 --> 00:01:44.960
And most concerningly,

00:01:44.960 --> 00:01:46.800
what if it’s causing
more inflammation

00:01:46.800 --> 00:01:49.360
in their artery walls?

00:01:49.360 --> 00:01:51.840
Indeed, there were
significantly greater amounts

00:01:51.840 --> 00:01:54.960
of athero-sclerotic plaque
in the individuals

00:01:54.960 --> 00:01:56.240
who had detectable levels

00:01:56.240 --> 00:01:59.920
of the anti-meat allergy
antibodies in their system.

00:01:59.920 --> 00:02:02.880
So, people who consume
mammalian meat

00:02:02.880 --> 00:02:04.440
appear to have
this chronic inflammation

00:02:04.440 --> 00:02:06.800
in the walls
of their coronary arteries

00:02:06.800 --> 00:02:08.560
that relates to this interaction

00:02:08.560 --> 00:02:11.120
between this α-Gal component
of meat

00:02:11.120 --> 00:02:13.520
and their anti-α-Gal antibodies

00:02:13.520 --> 00:02:16.320
if they’ve been bitten
by a tick.

00:02:16.320 --> 00:02:18.400
Those having a heart attack

00:02:18.400 --> 00:02:21.920
had about a whopping
13 times higher likelihood

00:02:21.920 --> 00:02:23.520
to having those antibodies,

00:02:23.520 --> 00:02:25.200
providing strong
supportive evidence

00:02:25.200 --> 00:02:26.720
for a clinically
important effect

00:02:26.720 --> 00:02:29.920
of α-Gal sensitization
on the development

00:02:29.920 --> 00:02:32.960
of coronary heart disease,
our leading cause of death,

00:02:32.960 --> 00:02:36.880
and acute myocardial infarction,
or heart attack.

00:02:36.880 --> 00:02:38.320
Okay, but wait a second.

00:02:38.320 --> 00:02:41.200
If having an asymptomatic
food allergy

00:02:41.200 --> 00:02:46.400
can so inflame our arteries,
what about other food allergies?

00:02:46.400 --> 00:02:50.080
An allergy to shrimp is actually
the most common food allergy

00:02:50.080 --> 00:02:50.960
in the United States,

00:02:50.960 --> 00:02:53.120
affecting up
to 1 in 50 Americans,

00:02:53.120 --> 00:02:55.840
but those are the people
who experience symptoms.

00:02:55.840 --> 00:02:59.520
Might a shrimp allergy
actually be affecting more?

00:02:59.520 --> 00:03:01.840
People with symptomatic
seafood allergies

00:03:01.840 --> 00:03:03.040
tend to know they are allergic,

00:03:03.040 --> 00:03:05.280
and know to just stay away
from shrimp.

00:03:05.280 --> 00:03:06.960
But some people
with shrimp allergies

00:03:06.960 --> 00:03:08.400
react differently.

00:03:08.400 --> 00:03:10.560
Some have classic
allergy symptoms,

00:03:10.560 --> 00:03:12.160
like breaking out in hives,
swelling,

00:03:12.160 --> 00:03:13.680
and difficulty breathing,

00:03:13.680 --> 00:03:16.800
but others develop symptoms
that manifest hours later-

00:03:16.800 --> 00:03:19.280
gastrointestinal symptoms
like nausea,

00:03:19.280 --> 00:03:21.600
abdominal cramps, diarrhea,
and vomiting.

00:03:21.600 --> 00:03:24.000
So, some
shrimp-sensitive patients

00:03:24.000 --> 00:03:26.960
just have this kind
of gastrointestinal upset.

00:03:26.960 --> 00:03:29.520
But what about people
who are sensitized to shrimp,

00:03:29.520 --> 00:03:31.360
and they don’t even know it

00:03:31.360 --> 00:03:34.800
because they don’t
exhibit any symptoms?

00:03:34.800 --> 00:03:38.320
In individuals without
symptomatic food allergy,

00:03:38.320 --> 00:03:40.720
having allergy antibodies
in their blood

00:03:40.720 --> 00:03:42.400
targeting some food

00:03:42.400 --> 00:03:45.600
was considered
clinically irrelevant,

00:03:45.600 --> 00:03:46.560
but that was before

00:03:46.560 --> 00:03:50.400
those tick-induced meat
sensitization studies came out.

00:03:50.400 --> 00:03:53.760
So, researchers looked to see
if having allergy antibodies

00:03:53.760 --> 00:03:55.360
against other foods
was associated

00:03:55.360 --> 00:03:56.880
with cardiovascular mortality,

00:03:56.880 --> 00:03:59.680
and, indeed,
that’s just what they found.

00:03:59.680 --> 00:04:00.880
From blood tests,

00:04:00.880 --> 00:04:04.320
it appears about 1 in 25 people
is allergic to milk,

00:04:04.320 --> 00:04:05.920
whether they know it or not.

00:04:05.920 --> 00:04:08.320
And in these two large studies,

00:04:08.320 --> 00:04:10.400
those who had
the milk sensitivity

00:04:10.400 --> 00:04:12.080
had between 2
and nearly 4 times

00:04:12.080 --> 00:04:14.960
the risk of dying
from cardiovascular disease,

00:04:14.960 --> 00:04:18.080
but the worst
appeared to be shrimp.

00:04:18.080 --> 00:04:20.640
6% of Americans,
about 1 in 17,

00:04:20.640 --> 00:04:23.280
have anti-shrimp antibodies
in their blood,

00:04:23.280 --> 00:04:24.800
whether they know it or not,

00:04:24.800 --> 00:04:28.400
and those who do are 3.7 times
more likely to die

00:04:28.400 --> 00:04:34.080
of cardiovascular disease,
but only if they eat shrimp.

00:04:34.080 --> 00:04:36.240
Having anti-shrimp antibodies
doesn’t matter

00:04:36.240 --> 00:04:37.840
if you don’t eat shrimp.

00:04:37.840 --> 00:04:41.040
What about having a milk,
peanut, or egg sensitivity

00:04:41.040 --> 00:04:43.440
but not eating those foods?

00:04:43.440 --> 00:04:45.680
There were too few people
not eating those foods

00:04:45.680 --> 00:04:47.040
to actually calculate it,

00:04:47.040 --> 00:04:49.120
but enough people
don’t eat shrimp

00:04:49.120 --> 00:04:50.560
that researchers could see

00:04:50.560 --> 00:04:52.560
that having
anti-shrimp antibodies

00:04:52.560 --> 00:04:55.680
only mattered
if you kept eating shrimp.

00:04:55.680 --> 00:04:58.160
The thought
is that chronic oral exposure

00:04:58.160 --> 00:05:00.880
to foods we have hidden
allergy antibodies for

00:05:00.880 --> 00:05:02.400
can lead to chronic inflammation

00:05:02.400 --> 00:05:05.280
that can manifest
in our arteries.

00:05:05.280 --> 00:05:07.440
This definitely challenges
the current thinking

00:05:07.440 --> 00:05:09.040
that these kinds
of food sensitivities

00:05:09.040 --> 00:05:12.582
without overt allergy
is benign.

